OL,3,AWhy are UK borrowing costs rising and
OL,4,Awhat does it mean for me?
OL,5,
OL,6,FUK government borrowing costs have been
OL,7,Frising, with some now at their highest
OL,8,Flevel since 1998 as investors around
OL,9,Fthe world worry about inflation.
OL,11,FWhy is this happening and how does it
OL,12,Faffect you?
OL,14,FA bond is a bit like an IOU that can be
OL,15,Ftraded in the financial markets.
OL,17,FGovernments generally spend more than
OL,18,Fthey raise in tax so they borrow money
OL,19,Fto fill the gap, usually by selling
OL,20,Fbonds to investors.
